ally posted by <strong>Leandro16</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1237168-gentleman-s-guide-to-vampires-v5?p=1238832#post1238832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I expect that the Second Inquisition has some kind of supernatural patron like the Techocrazy wanting to hunt vampires after what happened in the week of nighmares with Kaiju-Ravnos becuase if not this doenst make any sense.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Maybe. Maybe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T05:08:55-07:00","id":1238871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1237168-gentleman-s-guide-to-vampires-v5?p=1238843#post1238843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Maybe. Maybe.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a shame really, Mr.Dawkins. You're quite good at the &quot;mysterious, tantalizing hint&quot; thing.<br /> <br /> Will it be a let-down, later this morning, when V5 is released and all the cats are out of all their bags?<br /> <br /> I'm picturing you at the front of the queue in your local take-out this afternoon: &quot;Hmmm, you want to know if I want red curry or white curry? Interesting questions, indeed. It could be either, really....&quot;<br /> <br /> Well, cheer up, there will always be another supplement to tease. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T05:22:53-07:00","id":1238875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gangrel44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1237168-gentleman-s-guide-to-vampires-v5?p=1238808#post1238808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are you telling me that a bunch of fanatical nutjobs managed to breach the Haus de Hexe in Vienna, and were able to whack The Council of Seven? Something that the Tzimisce, Gangrel, and Nosferatu were unable to do in the Dark Ages? Something does not add up here...</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't see the operation being carried out by a single guy who is only mildly interested and quite sane. &quot;Be a bunch of fanatical nutjobs&quot; is probably step-one in any plan that ends with the Council destroyed.<br /> <br /> Besides, I'd bet that there was some inside help from Saulot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T08:07:17-07:00","id":1238914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nosimplehiway</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1237168-gentleman-s-guide-to-vampires-v5?p=1238871#post1238871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's a shame really, Mr.Dawkins. You're quite good at the &quot;mysterious, tantalizing hint&quot; thing.<br /> <br /> Will it be a let-down, later this morning, when V5 is released and all the cats are out of all their bags?<br /> <br /> I'm picturing you at the front of the queue in your local take-out this afternoon: &quot;Hmmm, you want to know if I want red curry or white curry? Interesting questions, indeed. It could be either, really....&quot;<br /> <br /> Well, cheer up, there will always be another supplement to tease. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There's always another mystery to tease.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T09:11:15-07:00","id":1238941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gangrel44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1237168-gentleman-s-guide-to-vampires-v5?p=1238808#post1238808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you telling me that a bunch of fanatical nutjobs managed to breach the Haus de Hexe in Vienna, and were able to whack The Council of Seven? Something that the Tzimisce, Gangrel, and Nosferatu were unable to do in the Dark Ages? Something does not add up here...</div> </div> </div> </div>From all accounts published so far, the Second Inquistion are not fanatical nutjobs, but rather highly-trained government agents and military types using latest technology. So what can the Tremere do about an all-out tactical assault that is maybe backed up by aerial strikes? Also, the council itself is rather seldom is found in Vienna. I don't think that any vampire without Fortitude could withstand a missile attack. Those that can, will be cleaned up afterwards by tactical strike teams. Factor in that the government can move by day, and even the main chantry (Fortschritt?) won't stand a chance. Thaumaturgy despite all it's paths and rituals is no true magick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1681-murder-of-crows","name":"Murder-of-Crows","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1681_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T09:16:22-07:00","id":1238943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murder-of-Crows</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1237168-gentleman-s-guide-to-vampires-v5?p=1238941#post1238941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From all accounts published so far, the Second Inquistion are not fanatical nutjobs, but rather highly-trained government agents and military types using latest technology. So what can the Tremere do about an all-out tactical assault that is maybe backed up by aerial strikes? Also, the council itself is rather seldom is found in Vienna. I don't think that any vampire without Fortitude could withstand a missile attack. Those that can, will be cleaned up afterwards by tactical strike teams. Factor in that the government can move by day, and even the main chantry (Fortschritt?) won't stand a chance. Thaumaturgy despite all it's paths and rituals is no true magick.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could a vampire survive a direct missile strike? Not unless they're an Antediluvian.<br /> <br /> But we're talking about a heavily enchanted fortress, with masters of dark magical abilities. You're assuming the missile would strike the vampire in the first place. The best way to survive an attack is to not be hit. EDIT: I was unclear in my defense of the chantry. First of all, I'm not certain where it's located, but you can't do a missile strike in the center of a city without civilian casualties, and that's something you avoid. If it's isolated though, that's not an issue. However, the ground invasion can be very easily thwarted and it has nothing to do with weapons, but the people *holding* them. We've seen several examples of chantries with the whole &quot;non-euclidian geometry&quot; thing going on, where unwelcome guests get lost in loops of corridors that double back and twist on themselves. No amount of GPS and body cams are going to fix that. As far as a daylight attack, that's what the ghouls and defenses are for.<br /> <br /> Also, let's be blunt. Modern soldiers are not action movie heroes. They're normal people with some training and good gear. Humanity's strength is in its *numbers*. Vampires have been fighting off highly trained vampire hunters for centuries. Modern tech does give humanity an edge, but it doesn't make the soldiers invulnerable and able to One-Hit-Kill Methuselahs.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying a SpecOps team couldn't assault the chantry. I'm just pointing out that it's not a clear cut victory simply because they have better funding than the Society of Leopold. Casaulties should have been high, and a pyrrhic victory at best. If it's just a &quot;humanity, fuck yeah!&quot; rolf-stomp, then it's just stupid. So far, every major plot twist of 5E I've been exposed to strikes me as &quot;storytelling by fiat,&quot; rather than a natural development of the setting, barring the resurgence of an Inquisition as a concept.<br /> <br /> Plus, as someone already pointed out, the Council of Seven didn't *live* there, and meetings were irregular. The idea that they somehow got all seven is patently ridiculous.<br /> <br /> The more I hear about the 5E lore, the more it feels like the massive lore shift between 2nd and Revised, where the authors took a chainsaw to anything they didn't like from previous authors, and removed the elements with all the subtlety of your missile attack example. I may use the 5E rules, but methinks I'll use Beckett's Jyhad Diary as a starting point for my own lore, because I really don't like the 5E setting update so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3200,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3200-barachiel","user":"Barachiel","date":". 07-26-2018, 01:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3200-barachiel","name":"Barachiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3200_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T11:13:54-07:00","id":1238991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barachiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1237168-gentleman-s-guide-to-vampires-v5?p=1238943#post1238943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But we're talking about a heavily enchanted fortress, with masters of dark magical abilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>With the previously published material on Thaumaturgy it is simply not possible to construct a chantry defense that withstands several missile hits.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barachiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1237168-gentleman-s-guide-to-vampires-v5?p=1238943#post1238943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was unclear in my defense of the chantry. First of all, I'm not certain where it's located, but you can't do a missile strike in the center of a city without civilian casualties, and that's something you avoid.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would I avoid that? Simply tell people that it was terrorist attack (which would actually be playing into various conspiracy theories, by making them &quot;real&quot; within the setting of Masquerade). If you go that route, civilian casualties become a non-issue (yes, I am aware how cynical that is).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barachiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1237168-gentleman-s-guide-to-vampires-v5?p=1238943#post1238943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, let's be blunt. Modern soldiers are not action movie heroes. They're normal people with some training and good gear. Humanity's strength is in its *numbers*. Vampires have been fighting off highly trained vampire hunters for centuries. Modern tech does give humanity an edge, but it doesn't make the soldiers invulnerable and able to One-Hit-Kill Methuselahs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, in a game with vampires, modern highly-trained soldiers could be treated as action movie heroes. The vampires certainly are. And there has always been the fear of the elders about humans rising up against vampires. That's exactly what the Second Inquisition is. It doesn't come out of nowhere, it's a logical expansion of the setting, and it's one way the metaplot could go.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, there is nothing preventing you from using the rules but not the setting. I see this as an explicit option that was even mentioned as vaild way to treat V5 sometime last year by a developer or other.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1681-murder-of-crows","name":"Murder-of-Crows","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1681_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T11:39:17-07:00","id":1239000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murder-of-Crows</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1237168-gentleman-s-guide-to-vampires-v5?p=1238991#post1238991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why would I avoid that? Simply tell people that it was terrorist attack (which would actually be playing into various conspiracy theories, by making them &quot;real&quot; within the setting of Masquerade). If you go that route, civilian casualties become a non-issue (yes, I am aware how cynical that is).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Because Austria isn't a third-world country who can't do anything more than shake it's fist impotently. This is an EU member who won't take kindly to that. <br /> <br /> So far, your entire defense of this is &quot;missiles win&quot;, which I don't disagree. But I've seen nothing that says they hit the chantry with a missile and called it a day. I'm treating this as an actual military op on a target in a major civilian center, which requires a ground team.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3200-barachiel","name":"Barachiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3200_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T11:45:53-07:00","id":1239004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barachiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1237168-gentleman-s-guide-to-vampires-v5?p=1239000#post1239000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because Austria isn't a third-world country who can't do anything more than shake it's fist impotently. This is an EU member who won't take kindly to that.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it is a government operation in the first place, and the terrorist angle a cover-up, then nothing will come of that. Second Inquisition is government operated as far as we know, and it's active world-wide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1681-murder-of-crows","name":"Murder-of-Crows","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1681_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T11:48:09-07:00","id":1239008,"title":"","content":"The Tremere organization, and the fact that they meet up is actually a weakness if your willing to go full on assault. Saulot always gets bored and whacks his kids.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T11:54:11-07:00","id":1239010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murder-of-Crows</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1237168-gentleman-s-guide-to-vampires-v5?p=1239004#post1239004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If it is a government operation in the first place, and the terrorist angle a cover-up, then nothing will come of that. Second Inquisition is government operated as far as we know, and it's active world-wide.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but here's the thing: they don't do that. The only time you *ever* hear of missile strikes on a city is during in an active war zone. There aren't news reports of NATO blowing up a terrorist cell in Paris with missiles because... follow me here, they don't do that. Could they do that ,and try to claim that? Sure! And they'd be roasted alive in the media, social and professional, families of nearby victims would sue and protest and the fallout would be *horrible.*<br /> <br /> No government agency would do that, when they can achieve the same result (so they think) with a surgical strike from a ground team. Because guess what? If lives are cheap, as you maintain, then its easier and cheaper to sacrifice a few soldiers, who signed up to go and die for their country, than to kill dozens or hundreds of civilians who can make the whole thing a PR nightmare. Plus, missiles are insanely expensive. There are always more grunts (again, coming from the cold, impersonal, numbers-game mindset).<br /> <br /> It's much easier to maintain a cover-up of soldiers dying in a perfectly normal &quot;nothing to see here&quot; operation, than trying to spin something insanely high profile like a missile strike in a major city. There are rules of engagement, and even the anti-terrorist groups don't get to casually ignore them with impunity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3200,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3200-barachiel","user":"Barachiel","date":". 07-26-2018, 02:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3200-barachiel","name":"Barachiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3200_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T12:37:51-07:00","id":1239022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barachiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1237168-gentleman-s-guide-to-vampires-v5?p=1239010#post1239010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, but here's the thing: they don't do that. The only time you *ever* hear of missile strikes on a city is during in an active war zone. There aren't news reports of NATO blowing up a terrorist cell in Paris with missiles because... follow me here, they don't do that. Could they do that ,and try to claim that? Sure! And they'd be roasted alive in the media, social and professional, families of nearby victims would sue and protest and the fallout would be *horrible.*</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you misunderstand what I am trying to say: government ops blows up Vienna chantry in massive operation. Officially, they blame the incident on terrorists, as in: terrorists did this - not as in: we did this to stop terrorists. So, officially, terrorists blew up some buildings in Vienna, not the government. Cover-up is in place, media outrage follows, and maybe in the EU somebody holds a speech against terrorism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1681-murder-of-crows","name":"Murder-of-Crows","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1681_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T12:41:08-07:00","id":1239023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murder-of-Crows</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1237168-gentleman-s-guide-to-vampires-v5?p=1239022#post1239022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you misunderstand what I am trying to say: government ops blows up Vienna chantry in massive operation. Officially, they blame the incident on terrorists, as in: terrorists did this - not as in: we did this to stop terrorists. So, officially, terrorists blew up some buildings in Vienna, not the government. Cover-up is in place, media outrage follows, and maybe in the EU somebody holds a speech against terrorism.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, that's somewhat different. Yes, I did misunderstand.<br /> <br /> But if that's the in-game explanation, then the writing for 5E is as bad as I feared. *cancels pre-order* If I want to read sloppy, hack writing then I'll go back to watching the CW. My tolerance for this crap has reached its nadir. And its not the plot ideas by itself. Its that they decide to arrive at said plot points by the laziest, most cliched manner possible, when with a little thought and effort, they could achieve their ends in an interesting manner.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3200-barachiel","name":"Barachiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3200_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T13:57:21-07:00","id":1239041,"title":"","content":"Besides armed men, some True Faith might be involved, thus countering Thaumaturgy. They are the Second Inquisition, after all. There is very few things vampires can do against True Faith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/412-valismedsen","name":"valismedsen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T14:35:57-07:00","id":1239049,"title":"","content":"I'd wait until I read the whole story, but at first glance, based on the interview, both London's falling and the beheading of the Tremere in Vienna is, honestly, and I'm sad I have to say that, sorry, but more than a little straining.<br /> <br /> In the case of London: yeah-yeah, it's the most-surveilled city of the world... So what? Crime, gang crime specifically is still record-high right now, if I understood correctly. Even if I take the Technocracy into account and even if all the mentioned* agencies were working together... Even if the whole thing was an inner job, machinations of Mithras who underestimated the mortals... Even then, in my oppinion, a good bunch of kindreds could have fled. Also, when was this, in the 10-year gap? If it was years back, maybe more than 5 years, the assumption that those agencies could maintain total control and the vampires wasn't able to seep back, to some extent is... More than straining. <br /> <br /> *About all the agencies: I'm not sure that the Leopold society helped here, but if yes, I dunno, Great Britain is very much not a catholic country, I'm not convinced they'd play well with the government spooks there (flashbacks to Hellsing...).<br /> <br /> Vienna: okay, no. Just no. Blowing up the Vienna chantry, okay, I could get that, if it was a massive operation. It has interesting story follow-up possibilities with the white worm and all. That the clan is fractured among Saulot-as-Tremere loyalist Tremeres, Goratrix-Tremere loyalists and &quot;free&quot; Carna-ists is a good idea, IMO. One of my biggest problems with the Tremere was always the pyramid itslef, because I don1t like to play characters in an organization like that. I assume the writers had the same idea, making the Tremere less bound, giving the players more freedom. That's okay. My problem is, if the &quot;beheading of the clan&quot; means the thing others argued about above, that the whole, or most of the councl is wiped out, that is, IMO, highly-highly unlikely, to the point of breaking verisimilitude.<br /> <br /> Overall. The two story points would be okay on themselves and as I said, I'll wait for making my final oppinion on the topic,until I've read the whole. BUT, hoestly, the whole thing feels like they really-really wanted to drive home the point that &quot;the Second Inquisition is SCAAAAARYYYY!!!! Whooooo!&quot;. I can't help but feel that they're way overplaying humans. maybe because if the Second Inquisition is <i>that</i> scary, that really justifies all the heavy setting changes ( the word &quot;Spellplague&quot; surfaced in my barin, for some nebulous reason...), but I don't like that, because it's really stretching as I see it at this point, even to the point of feeling forced. Sure, humans could screw vampires a lot, if they start to pay attention, but it just feels too over-the-top. I just don't believe powerfull methuselahs would be that oblivious and powerless. I'm not even talking about a straight fight (although I really think they'd have ample tools to at least flee), but to avoid it, or counter the worst of it. I don't think the whole Tremere leadership would fall to an attack, even if they'd lose the main chantry (which would be a great loss, no doubt) and I don't think any agancy could keep all the vampires out of a city the size and population of London, for long, even if they could drive out them for a short time and undoubtedly destroying quite a few of them during the process.<br /> <br /> So, that's my 2 cent, at this point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T15:41:55-07:00","id":1239059,"title":"","content":"I get why people who like the Tremere don't like the council going down.<br /> <br /> That said, the thing about London is pretty believable, with all the spying ability modern technology gives us, that I could see pretty easy. I think truly defensive Kindred could escape for sure, but most of them going down in a 1 day raid situation seems pretty plausible.<br /> The information we give away on a regular basis, the fact that all communication can be monitored and Vampires basic lack of understanding.<br /> <br /> Once they found some they could follow vamps back from Elysium with technology and the Kindred having no idea they were being tracked or the call was listened too or just the crazy paper trail they leave doing everyday things. Who did they email or even mail.<br /> <br /> It's the old Batman argument. In today's world he couldn't exist, full stop. &quot;This is the satellite and traffic cam footage of the Batmobile driving back to Wayne Manor&quot; etc...<br /> <br /> Vampires should be heading to South America and Africa to be honest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T16:21:52-07:00","id":1239071,"title":"","content":"There's really no need to be concerned. An in-game narrator says the entire Council of Seven fell, but who's raking through the ashes to find out? Maybe Meerlinda went to ground while the heat was on, maybe Etrius didn't show up that night. As they're Methuselahs, it's unlikely protagonists will interact with them anyway, so resolving their fates is not a priority in the first three releases. Far better to leave a lot of conjecture and worst guesses in the World of Darkness while they're waiting for the fallout to settle.<br /> <br /> The same goes for London. Did every Kindred in London perish? Definitely not. But is London considered empty of Kindred now? Yes. The Camarilla states the city was purged. That doesn't mean Anarch packs, small coteries, or hiding elders aren't still there. What it means is as far as the world's vampires are concerned, it's a hot zone. Do not visit. That makes for an interesting city to place in a chronicle, at least in my opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T17:25:51-07:00","id":1239091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vamps Like Us</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1237168-gentleman-s-guide-to-vampires-v5?p=1239059#post1239059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get why people who like the Tremere don't like the council going down.<br /> <br /> That said, the thing about London is pretty believable, with all the spying ability modern technology gives us, that I could see pretty easy. I think truly defensive Kindred could escape for sure, but most of them going down in a 1 day raid situation seems pretty plausible.<br /> The information we give away on a regular basis, the fact that all communication can be monitored and Vampires basic lack of understanding.<br /> <br /> Once they found some they could follow vamps back from Elysium with technology and the Kindred having no idea they were being tracked or the call was listened too or just the crazy paper trail they leave doing everyday things. Who did they email or even mail.<br /> <br /> It's the old Batman argument. In today's world he couldn't exist, full stop. &quot;This is the satellite and traffic cam footage of the Batmobile driving back to Wayne Manor&quot; etc...<br /> <br /> Vampires should be heading to South America and Africa to be honest.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, but no. That's the exact thing people are arguning about for a time, regarding the Masquerade, that we're living in a world where everyone has a HD camera and there are surveillance, etc. No, sorry to say that, but technology isn't omnipotent. Despite all the above things, crime exists, organized crime exists, hell, <i>terrorism</i> exists even in the first world and London actually has a worse violent crime record than New York <i>right now</i> and gang knife violence is a big problem there, just as attacks with acid, etc. It's just a huge city, with a stupendous ammount of people and n no way I will believe that even the up-and-mighty Technocracy itslef would be able to keep <i>all</i> the vampires out for a prolonged period. That they could hit hard the local Camarilla, who've grown complacent and drive out or kill most of them? Sure, that's plausible. That they could keep it that way is ridiculous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T17:33:23-07:00","id":1239097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barachiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1237168-gentleman-s-guide-to-vampires-v5?p=1238943#post1238943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus, as someone already pointed out, the Council of Seven didn't *live* there, and meetings were irregular. The idea that they somehow got all seven is patently ridiculous.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if they were all there for a meeting (Which is the perfect time to strike), they would all have escape to true friend or some variant where they could teleport to one of numerous safe houses in an instant. Probably an autotrigger version that recognises imminent danger thanks to; oh wait Auspex foresight.<br /> <br /> As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar152_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"152\" data-vbnamecard=\"152\">The Gentleman Gamer</a> mentioned; the pyramid has been destroyed, but individuals could have survived. Elders with 7+ Auspex probably sent in decoys at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T17:37:24-07:00","id":1239101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1237168-gentleman-s-guide-to-vampires-v5?p=1239071#post1239071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's really no need to be concerned. An in-game narrator says the entire Council of Seven fell, but who's raking through the ashes to find out? Maybe Meerlinda went to ground while the heat was on, maybe Etrius didn't show up that night. As they're Methuselahs, it's unlikely protagonists will interact with them anyway, so resolving their fates is not a priority in the first three releases. Far better to leave a lot of conjecture and worst guesses in the World of Darkness while they're waiting for the fallout to settle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Although, I assume there is still a &quot;loyalist&quot; faction among the three, so I'd argue that the question of how many of their superiors are still around, giving commands and organizing things is a rather important one. I get the whole &quot;unreliable narrator&quot; thing and most of the time, I like it. But i think unlikely that those methuselahs would just hang up their robes and go away enjoying the hot Malibou nights and some fishing. I suspect they'd be over their head trying to sort out the whole mess and don't waste a minute reassuring their subordinates that yes, they're still around, to prevent even more chaos.<br /> <br /> I get that this edition's main theme seems to be &quot;everything is falling apart&quot; and overall, I'm okay with that, but in places, it's a bit straining and I'm sorry to say that, because I tend to very much like your writing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The same goes for London. Did every Kindred in London perish? Definitely not. But is London considered empty of Kindred now? Yes. The Camarilla states the city was purged. That doesn't mean Anarch packs, small coteries, or hiding elders aren't still there. What it means is as far as the world's vampires are concerned, it's a hot zone. Do not visit. That makes for an interesting city to place in a chronicle, at least in my opinion. </div> </div> </div>That's way more sensible. I'd be okay with it being a dangerous place, where you really need to watch your steps and where the Camarilla holds no domain (at least not physically, I doubt they'd stay completely out of one of the biggest financial centres of the world). I agree, that makes it an interesting place for a chronicle. &quot;Reclaiming London&quot;. I like it, much potential. I just thought that, while offing the previous Cam establishment (and likely most of the non-Cam) here is totally possible, with enough resources, careful planning and yes, leaked information and too overly uppity elders, keeping out all vampires is definitely not.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T17:57:47-07:00","id":1239116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1237168-gentleman-s-guide-to-vampires-v5?p=1239091#post1239091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry, but no. That's the exact thing people are arguning about for a time, regarding the Masquerade, that we're living in a world where everyone has a HD camera and there are surveillance, etc. No, sorry to say that, but technology isn't omnipotent. Despite all the above things, crime exists, organized crime exists, hell, <i>terrorism</i> exists even in the first world and London actually has a worse violent crime record than New York <i>right now</i> and gang knife violence is a big problem there, just as attacks with acid, etc. It's just a huge city, with a stupendous ammount of people and n no way I will believe that even the up-and-mighty Technocracy itslef would be able to keep <i>all</i> the vampires out for a prolonged period. That they could hit hard the local Camarilla, who've grown complacent and drive out or kill most of them? Sure, that's plausible. That they could keep it that way is ridiculous.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was arguing for the initial strike taking out so many. I think few Vampires could survive a surprise raid at 8 in the morning on a cloudless day. The crime exists isn't the same as powerful government agency devoting huge resources to target a small group and pounce when they think they have them all in cross hairs. The government does this to terrorist cells now. I just think a city wide surprise raid one day would devastate the population if they gathered info for say a year. How many Kindred realized they walked around with a GPS locator and every call they took potentially put them under scrutiny and then every call they made did so to others.<br /> <br /> Your right people could go back to London. Why would you? but you could. You'd be better off in the country side with some loyal ghouls herd then running back into a war zone that killed most of your friends.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T18:07:53-07:00","id":1239121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vamps Like Us</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1237168-gentleman-s-guide-to-vampires-v5?p=1239116#post1239116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was arguing for the initial strike taking out so many. I think few Vampires could survive a surprise raid at 8 in the morning on a cloudless day. The crime exists isn't the same as powerful government agency devoting huge resources to target a small group and pounce when they think they have them all in cross hairs. The government does this to terrorist cells now. I just think a city wide surprise raid one day would devastate the population if they gathered info for say a year. How many Kindred realized they walked around with a GPS locator and every call they took potentially put them under scrutiny and then every call they made did so to others.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, we're practically both saying that the initial raid is possible, but they wouldn't be able to maintain it, I guess.<br /> <br /> My main point was: people tend to frame technology as the be-all-end-all thing that'd made clandestine things impossible. Sorry, but we are not yet here, thanks to everyone who might listen. Yes it reduced bad things a lot, but they're still there.<br /> <br /> Like, depsiute all the technology, all the resources, Terrorist attacks still happened in London. As I said, crime and organized crime <i>is still </i><i>hapening</i> and a big problem, in the most surveilled city of the world. Vampires could manage it, but I could agree, that if the old guard have grown over-confident and information were leaked, that could possibly end up as a very nasty morning...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Your right people could go back to London. Why would you? but you could. You'd be better off in the country side with some loyal ghouls herd then running back into a war zone that killed most of your friends. </div> </div> </div>Maybe not the same people (although I think surviving elders might want to reclaim their old domains and resources). But London is HUGE. Huge ammount of people (many of them immignrants, from Eastern Europe, the Middle East, and all over the World, who don't really cause a blip on anyone's radar, if they disappear, so plenty of potential food), businesses, places to hide. With the old guard down, I'd imagine new vampires trying it out, in droves, after the initial dust settled. It's just too big of a fruit to not be taken (or at least tried to be) by anyone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 07-26-2018, 09:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T18:52:15-07:00","id":1239140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1237168-gentleman-s-guide-to-vampires-v5?p=1239101#post1239101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's way more sensible. I'd be okay with it being a dangerous place, where you really need to watch your steps and where the Camarilla holds no domain (at least not physically, I doubt they'd stay completely out of one of the biggest financial centres of the world). I agree, that makes it an interesting place for a chronicle. &quot;Reclaiming London&quot;. I like it, much potential. I just thought that, while offing the previous Cam establishment (and likely most of the non-Cam) here is totally possible, with enough resources, careful planning and yes, leaked information and too overly uppity elders, keeping out all vampires is definitely not.</div> </div> </div> </div>A campaign about the <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Camarilla taking back London (and other places lost in the last 20 years) sounds really cool.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12439-the-vampire-fish","name":"The Vampire Fish","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12439_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T19:25:52-07:00","id":1239155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illithid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1237168-gentleman-s-guide-to-vampires-v5?p=1239097#post1239097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if they were all there for a meeting (Which is the perfect time to strike), they would all have escape to true friend or some variant where they could teleport to one of numerous safe houses in an instant. Probably an autotrigger version that recognises imminent danger thanks to; oh wait Auspex foresight.<br /> <br /> As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar152_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"152\" data-vbnamecard=\"152\">The Gentleman Gamer</a> mentioned; the pyramid has been destroyed, but individuals could have survived. Elders with 7+ Auspex probably sent in decoys at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>All good points, but ultimately, I shouldn't have to do the mental gymnastics to justify their poorly thought-out writing choices, when I can tear it apart with far less effort.<br /> <br /> Here, let me conjure you up a better version off the top of my head. Or maybe it's been brewing in the back of my mind the last 6 hours since I first found this thread.<br /> <br /> The Inquisition 2: Electric Boogaloo identifies some members of the Council of Seven. They strike out at one, who barely escapes, and flees to Vienna. This gets the chantry highlighted with direct surveillance. Some of the other council members show up to discuss the situation. The trigger happy mortals go in, guns blazing. Realizing they've been found out, the Council elects to blow up their own chantry, and &quot;fake&quot; their deaths as far as the mortals are concerned. The Council also decides against meeting again in any formal capacity until they're sure they're not being tracked. With the hierarchy disrupted (not destroyed), factions break off into mini-houses and try to go their own way. Meanwhile, the Council struggles to regain control.<br /> <br /> BOOM! Gets the story points they want out there, and does so in a clear logical fashion that treats all sides as competent. See how easy it is? Why should I put more effort into justifying the game's story choices than the writers did in creating it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3200,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3200-barachiel","user":"Barachiel","date":". 07-26-2018, 11:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3200-barachiel","name":"Barachiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3200_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T08:46:59-07:00","id":1239324,"title":"","content":"While I think this scenario would be acceptable, an indipendent human organization trying to start a serious violent clash in an european city is doomed for failure even before firing a single round. The statal police and army will crack down on them even as they catch a whiff of firearms imported in the country (I don't remember the Austrian stance in this matters, but many european countries frown when a lot of firearms are in the hands of non-military personnel).<br /> Therefore I can think of two scenarios:<br /> 1- The conflict is at low intensity. No assaults but a lot of &quot;single accidents&quot; happening at the same times to different Tremere holdings while a picked squad penetrates the stronghold using less-than-conspicuous weapons. The damage they can do is evidently on the lower end of the spectrum, probably they can kill many ghouls and low (or even middle) tier Tremere, but the Fantastic Seven just fake their deaths and go into hiding.<br /> 2- The group is backed by members of the Austrian government / military / whatever group. This helps mantaining civilian and interlopers away from the conflict zones and maybe bringing in stronger weapons, but not really that much as a government-related group would prefer to downplay any operation of this kind, so explosives / firearms and the like would certainly be restricted (or allowed only if silenced, at the best). Nonetheless this would allow of a higher level of damage, and probably at least some high-tier Tremere would end their unlives there (maybe even a Councillor or two).<br /> <br /> The most important part, however, is not Sandworm-Saulot. We already know that humans can't kill an antediluvian, even in a weakened state.<br /> The point is that below Vienna's Chantry are kepts vials of thaumathurgically preserved vitae of each and every Tremere ever existed (at least, the remaining ones after Goratrix's flight to the Sabbat). So, if the Vienna's Chantry is gone, that blood is gone... or was taken away.<br /> This can also mean that, maybe, this &quot;human&quot; organization may have some supernatural mastermind well accostumed to Tremere's rituals and defenses.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ed6RV6Z.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div></div> </div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","name":"Ryoga84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T09:57:15-07:00","id":1239349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryoga84</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1237168-gentleman-s-guide-to-vampires-v5?p=1239324#post1239324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The point is that below Vienna's Chantry are kepts vials of thaumathurgically preserved vitae of each and every Tremere ever existed (at least, the remaining ones after Goratrix's flight to the Sabbat). So, if the Vienna's Chantry is g